course: dictionary
lesson: 4303
title: Context clues and the griot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a new word. They often give clues to its meaning. Read this: «The kora is a West African instrument, traditionally played by griots, who keep history through song.» The words played, keep history and song are the clues. A griot must be someone who plays music and tells history.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit in the sentence. Then try your meaning in place of the hard word. Try this: «Griots keep history alive by telling it aloud.» If you put in a storyteller who sings and shares the past, the sentence still makes sense. So griot means that kind of person.
explain: Griots live in West Africa, in places such as Mali, Senegal, The Gambia and Guinea. In these places, history was often passed on by memory and speech, not only in books. Griots were the people who carried it.
fact: A griot is a traditional storyteller, singer, poet and historian in West Africa.
fact: Griots keep the history of families and peoples alive by telling it aloud, often with music.
fact: Griots often play the kora, a harp-like instrument with 21 strings.
fact: Griots tell the story of Sundiata Keita, founder of the Mali Empire.
fact: History was passed down by memory and speech, not only in books, and griots are a key part of this tradition.
exercise: «...traditionally played by griots, who keep history through song.» What do griots do? | Sell food at the market | Build houses from gourds | Write all their history in books | * Tell and sing history aloud
exercise: Griots often play the kora. What is a kora? | A kind of bread | A harp-like instrument with 21 strings | A large drum from the sea | * A harp-like instrument with 21 strings
exercise: Griots tell the story of Sundiata Keita. What did he found? | * The Mali Empire | The Ottoman Empire | The Roman Empire | A school in London
test: Griots kept history alive without books. How was history passed down? | Only by writing it in books | * By memory and speech | By radio broadcasts only | By drawing maps
test: Which country is in West Africa, where griots are found? | Sweden | Japan | * Senegal | Peru
exam: What does «griot» mean? | A harp with 42 strings | * A traditional storyteller, singer, poet and historian of West Africa | A famous king of the Mali Empire | A kind of gourd used for water
